-- Same 40-Region/67-edge instance as valid-instance.soil, EXCEPT R38's
-- color is set to 1 instead of 2 -- R38 has exactly ONE neighbor in this
-- fixed graph (R37, color 1: see the single (r37,r38) edge in
-- GraphColoring.properties), so this is the minimal possible change that
-- deliberately violates properColoring for exactly one adjacent pair and
-- nothing else. USE checks a class invariant as a single
-- Region.allInstances->forAll statement, so `check -v` reports this as one
-- failed invariant overall (confirmed: "checked 2 invariants ..., 1
-- failure") -- its -v trace does walk both R37 and R38's own
-- r.neighbor->forAll sub-evaluations (each finds the other with a matching
-- color), but that is one wrong edge surfacing in the trace from both
-- sides, not two separate failures.
--
-- noSelfLoop is unaffected (still holds for every Region, same as
-- valid-instance.soil) -- this fixture isolates properColoring alone.

!create r0 : Region
!set r0.name := 'R0'
!set r0.color := 1
